          "message": {
            "text": "The post-selection run boundary is the consolidation point shared by paths and embedded-font modes: fallback has already selected the exact face and UTF-16 span, then every supported run receives the same Chromium-configured HarfBuzz proxy. This keeps native/fontkit APIs as outline/metric providers without letting them choose glyphs.",
            "markdown": "The post-selection run boundary is the consolidation point shared by paths and embedded-font modes: fallback has already selected the exact face and UTF-16 span, then every supported run receives the same Chromium-configured HarfBuzz proxy. This keeps native/fontkit APIs as outline/metric providers without letting them choose glyphs."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/render/cluster-fallback.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1002,
                  "endLine": 1016,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "      if (aDecomposed) last.decomposed = true;\n    } else {\n      runs.push({ fontKey: a.key, font: a.font, text: aText, startIdx: a.start, endIdx: a.end, isPrimary: a.isPrimary, ...(aDecomposed ? { decomposed: true } : {}) });\n    }\n  }\n  // Production shaping is consolidated on the Chromium-configured HarfBuzz\n  // build after face selection and fallback assignment. Applied AFTER merging\n  // so the wrap sees whole runs; the proxy\n  // is memoized per (base instance, args), so identical bases keep a stable\n  // identity — the renderer's run-grouping invariant. Native/fontkit objects\n  // remain outline and metric providers only; they no longer decide glyphs.\n  for (const run of runs) {\n    run.font = harfbuzzShapedRunOverride(run.font, run.fontKey, weight, fontSize, slant, run.isPrimary ? variationSettings : undefined, run.text, opts?.features);\n  }\n  return runs;"
                  }
                }
