          "guid": "mt33ihkj87f6sy3i",
          "message": {
            "text": "The default route must keep Blink FontFallbackIterator as the sole assignment owner. Chromium 7d859f27 shapes every queued range through ShapeRange and commits or requeues complete clusters; HarfBuzz 4de187d decides canonical normalization and broken-syllable U+25CC insertion against the current candidate face. Pre-pinning a mark face, committing replacement text, or restarting per codepoint bypasses that ownership.",
            "markdown": "The default route must keep Blink FontFallbackIterator as the sole assignment owner. Chromium 7d859f27 shapes every queued range through ShapeRange and commits or requeues complete clusters; HarfBuzz 4de187d decides canonical normalization and broken-syllable U+25CC insertion against the current candidate face. Pre-pinning a mark face, committing replacement text, or restarting per codepoint bypasses that ownership."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/render/cluster-fallback.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 41,
                  "endLine": 53,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "// Enabled by default; `DOMOTION_CLUSTER_FALLBACK=0` restores the per-codepoint\n// walk only as an explicit A/B mutation. The default route never changes its\n// assignment algorithm because one candidate cannot be opened by our HarfBuzz\n// bridge. Such a candidate stays in FontFallbackIterator order, its range stays\n// queued, and the terminal still belongs to Blink's first candidate.\n//\n// Dotted-circle insertion and canonical decomposition deliberately have no\n// prepass here. They are outcomes of shaping each selected candidate:\n// `hb_syllabic_insert_dotted_circles` first requires a broken syllable AND that\n// candidate's U+25CC glyph (`hb-ot-shaper-syllabic.cc:33-99`, rev 4de187d),\n// while `decompose_current_character` tests the source scalar and canonical\n// pieces in the same candidate (`hb-ot-shape-normalize.cc:108-200`). Committing\n// either result before `ShapeRange` bypasses the state machine that owns it."
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
